  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Sat May 30 2026\n\nHot temperatures return to west central Texas from Sunday into \nTuesday next week, as upper-level ridging build across the area \nand high temperatures climb back into the 90s. Warmest \ntemperatures are expected across the Big Country with some areas \nnearing the 100 degree mark. Models show the upper-level ridge \nbegin to breakdown Tuesday through the remainder of the week and \ninto next weekend, as a series of upper-level disturbances track \nthrough the area from the north and west and upper level troughing\nsettles into the area. This will transition the area into a more \nactive pattern with increased showers and thunderstorm chances \nthrough this time period. Chances for precipitation remain low to \nmedium (20%-50%) each day Wednesday through next weekend, with a \ngood amount of uncertainty in coverage and intensity given the \nweak troughing and ongoing discrepancies in the timing of the \ndisturbances. However, the increased precipitation chances and \nample cloud cover will keep high temperatures cooler from \nWednesday through Friday at least, with temperatures remaining in \nthe 80s to low 90s. Temperatures begin to gradually increase back \ninto the 90s next weekend as upper-level ridging begins to build \nback across the region.",
